  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Change of use from two flats to single dwelling house; Erection of three storey rear extension at lower ground, ground floor and first floor; new terrace at first floor; erection of mansard roof extension and alterations to rear windows.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-2092f317-7fff-b918-0eca-53b8dda5dd1e&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of its detailed design, appearance, and form, results in an inappropriate solid-to-void ratio that would fail &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;to respect the architectural character of the original host building and the setting of the wider terrace, which it forms part of. Furthermore, the proposed glazing to the rear lower ground and ground floors fails to conserve or enhance and reveal the significance of the adjoining locally listed building at no.42 Clissold Crescent and impacts its setting.  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;As such, the proposal is contrary to the policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP4 (Non-Designated Heritage Assets) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan LP33 (2020) and policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) and D4 (Delivering good design) and HC1 (Conservation heritage and growth) of The London Plan (2021) and the advice contained within Hackney&#x27;s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
